WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:22.500
OSHA 10 is not optional. You need this to work on most commercial job sites.

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:45.000
Fire prevention and hot work permits. Brazing and soldering create fire hazards.
Hot work permits are required when working near combustible materials. A fire
watch must be maintained for 30 minutes after hot work is completed. Fire

00:00:45.000 --> 00:01:07.500
Here are the key terms. Write these down.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:30.000
Hot Work Permit: Required authorization for brazing, welding, or soldering near
combustible materials.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:52.500
PASS: Fire extinguisher technique: Pull, Aim, Squeeze, Sweep.

00:01:52.500 --> 00:02:15.000
Here's why this matters on the job: HVAC technicians braze copper tubing
regularly. Fire prevention is part of every brazing job.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:37.500
Watch out for these: Fire watch for 30 minutes after hot work. And — Know which
extinguisher for which fire type

